## 5. DATABASE (PostgreSQL)

Plain `.sql` migration files in `server/src/db/migrations/` applied by a tiny runner (`npm run migrate`) that records applied files in a `schema_migrations` table. Use `TEXT` with `CHECK` constraints instead of enum types (easier to change later).

### 5.1 Tables

**users**: `id SERIAL PK`, `username TEXT UNIQUE NOT NULL`, `password_hash TEXT NOT NULL`, `role TEXT CHECK IN ('passenger','driver','admin')`, `name TEXT`, `phone TEXT`, `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()`

**drivers**: `id SERIAL PK`, `user_id INT UNIQUE REFERENCES users`, `vehicle_type TEXT CHECK IN ('AUTO','HATCHBACK','SEDAN','SUV')`, `vehicle_number TEXT`, `lat DOUBLE PRECISION`, `lng DOUBLE PRECISION`, `status TEXT CHECK IN ('OFFLINE','AVAILABLE','BUSY') DEFAULT 'OFFLINE'`, `online_since TIMESTAMPTZ`, `last_heartbeat TIMESTAMPTZ`, `offers_received INT DEFAULT 0`, `rides_completed INT DEFAULT 0`, `accept_rate NUMERIC(3,2) DEFAULT 0.80`

**rides**: `id SERIAL PK`, `passenger_id INT REFERENCES users`, `pickup_lat, pickup_lng, pickup_label`, `drop_lat, drop_lng, drop_label`, `vehicle_type TEXT NULL`, `status TEXT CHECK IN ('REQUESTED','DRIVER_OFFERED','ACCEPTED','ARRIVING','ONGOING','COMPLETED','UNFULFILLED','CANCELLED')`, `version INT DEFAULT 0`, `attempt_count INT DEFAULT 0`, `current_driver_id INT NULL REFERENCES drivers`, `trip_distance_km NUMERIC`, `trip_duration_min NUMERIC`, `estimated_pickup_eta_min NUMERIC`, `estimated_fare NUMERIC`, `final_fare NUMERIC`, `fare_breakdown JSONB`, `zone_id TEXT NULL`, `created_at`, `accepted_at`, `arriving_at`, `started_at`, `completed_at`, `cancelled_at`

**offers**: `id SERIAL PK`, `ride_id INT REFERENCES rides`, `driver_id INT REFERENCES drivers`, `status TEXT CHECK IN ('PENDING','ACCEPTED','REJECTED','EXPIRED')`, `expires_at TIMESTAMPTZ`, `version INT DEFAULT 0`, `rank_position INT`, `score NUMERIC`, `decision_id TEXT`, `created_at`, `responded_at`

**ride_events**: `id BIGSERIAL PK`, `event_id UUID UNIQUE DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()`, `event_type TEXT`, `ride_id INT`, `driver_id INT NULL`, `offer_id INT NULL`, `payload JSONB DEFAULT '{}'`, `occurred_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()`

**notifications**: `id SERIAL PK`, `user_id INT REFERENCES users`, `ride_id INT NULL`, `message TEXT`, `read BOOLEAN DEFAULT false`, `created_at`

**idempotency_keys**: `key TEXT`, `user_id INT`, `endpoint TEXT`, `response_status INT`, `response_body JSONB`, `created_at`, `PRIMARY KEY (key, user_id, endpoint)`

### 5.2 Constraints that enforce the rules in the database
```sql
-- at most one pending offer per ride
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX one_pending_offer_per_ride ON offers(ride_id) WHERE status = 'PENDING';
-- never offer the same ride to the same driver twice
ALTER TABLE offers ADD CONSTRAINT one_offer_per_driver_per_ride UNIQUE (ride_id, driver_id);
-- one active ride per passenger
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX one_active_ride_per_passenger ON rides(passenger_id)
  WHERE status IN ('REQUESTED','DRIVER_OFFERED','ACCEPTED','ARRIVING','ONGOING');
-- a driver cannot be assigned to two active rides
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX one_active_ride_per_driver ON rides(current_driver_id)
  WHERE current_driver_id IS NOT NULL AND status IN ('ACCEPTED','ARRIVING','ONGOING');
```
Add indexes on `offers(status, expires_at)`, `rides(passenger_id, created_at)`, `ride_events(ride_id, occurred_at)`.

