## 10. EXTENSION POINTS (design for these; do NOT build the features now)

| Future feature | How it plugs in (no core rewrite) |
|---|---|
| **Fairness debt + multi-factor scoring** | New `rankers/fair.js`, `registerRanker("fair", ...)`, set `RANKER=fair`. Reads `driver.offersReceived`, `onlineSince`, `ridesCompleted`, `acceptRate` already on every candidate |
| **Explainable allocation** | `ScoredDriver.factors` and `reason` already flow to the API, events and DemoPanel |
| **Adaptive weights** | Weights from `ctx.config.weights`, `ctx.zone`, and `RANKER_WEIGHTS`; a function chooses a weight set per context |
| **Simulation (nearest vs fair)** | A headless script in `simulation/` imports `src/rankers` and `src/services/geo.js`, replays the same synthetic ride sequence through each ranker, computes Jain's index and waiting-time metrics |
| **Driver cancellation** | New route calling `recoverRide(rideId, "driver_cancelled")` plus a strategy entry; emits `DRIVER_CANCELLED` |
| **Delayed arrival** | A check calling `recoverRide(rideId, "delayed_arrival")`; strategy compares revised ETA against alternatives |
| **Driver offline detection** | Worker adds a check on `last_heartbeat`; calls `recoverRide(..., "driver_offline")` |
| **Radius expansion / repeated-failure escalation** | A strategy in `recoveryStrategies` that increases radius via `ctx` |
| **Zone intelligence / surge pricing** | Replace the stub in `zoneIntelligence.js` with an HTTP client; add the surge modifier to `fareModifiers` |
| **Extra eligibility constraints** (rating, documents, seats) | Add a rule to `eligibilityRules` |
| **Ride pooling** | New service consuming `RIDE_REQUESTED` from the event bus; a pool-aware ranker or pre-matching step |
| **Real-time updates** | Subscribe a Server-Sent Events/WebSocket broadcaster to `eventBus`; replace polling |
| **Kafka / external integration** | Subscribe a publisher to `eventBus`; events already carry `eventId` for idempotent consumers |
| **Ratings, payments, promo codes** | New tables and modifiers; the ride and fare pipelines do not change |
| **Teammates' services** | Their location/matching can call `POST /dispatch/allocate`; or replace the DB query inside `eligibility.js` |

**Do not implement now:** fairness scoring, adaptive weights, simulation, pooling, WebSockets, Kafka, Redis, payments, OTP/email verification.

